WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.280 --> 00:00:02.440
We all want to eat
the kinds of foods

00:00:02.440 --> 00:00:05.240
that make us feel
better and live longer.

00:00:05.240 --> 00:00:07.600
But there’s so much conflicting
information out there,

00:00:07.600 --> 00:00:10.960
so many nutrition opinions.

00:00:10.960 --> 00:00:13.680
Welcome to the
Nutrition Facts Podcast,

00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:15.560
I’m your host,
Dr. Michael Greger.

00:00:15.560 --> 00:00:17.800
It’s my job to give you
the information you need

00:00:17.800 --> 00:00:21.000
to make the healthiest
choices possible.

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:23.640
Today we hear about
dietary remedies

00:00:23.640 --> 00:00:28.640
that encourage mosquitos
and ticks to find a meal elsewhere.

00:00:28.640 --> 00:00:32.160
Are some people just more
attractive to mosquitos than others?

00:00:32.160 --> 00:00:33.960
Apparently so,
as identical twins

00:00:33.960 --> 00:00:36.960
are most likely
to be similarly tasty

00:00:36.960 --> 00:00:39.240
compared to fraternal
twins who only share

00:00:39.240 --> 00:00:40.880
50 percent of their DNA,

00:00:40.880 --> 00:00:45.440
demonstrating an underlying genetic
component that can be sniffed out

00:00:45.440 --> 00:00:47.880
by mosquitoes, although it’s
not clear if it’s because

00:00:47.880 --> 00:00:51.200
some people smell better
or other people just smell worse.

00:00:51.200 --> 00:00:55.080
We know pregnant women are twice
as attractive to malaria mosquitoes

00:00:55.080 --> 00:00:58.240
and also that mosquitoes
are attracted to sweat.

00:00:58.240 --> 00:01:01.840
Human sweat contains components
that are attractive to anthropophilic—

00:01:01.840 --> 00:01:05.120
meaning human-loving—
mosquitoes.

00:01:05.120 --> 00:01:08.320
The unique composition of human
sweat appears to explain

00:01:08.320 --> 00:01:11.600
its tantalizing effect, though sweat
from some body parts

00:01:11.600 --> 00:01:14.240
are evidently more
tantalizing than others.

00:01:14.240 --> 00:01:16.680
Skin emanations
collected from armpits

00:01:16.680 --> 00:01:19.420
were less attractive
compared to hands or feet.

00:01:19.420 --> 00:01:21.000
Here’s the graph. They think
the difference may be caused

00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:24.760
by deodorant residues,
since in a subsequent experiment,

00:01:24.760 --> 00:01:28.400
volunteers were asked to avoid using
skincare products for five days,

00:01:28.400 --> 00:01:31.880
and after that no
differences were detected.

00:01:31.880 --> 00:01:35.680
The creepiest bit
of research I found was this.

00:01:35.680 --> 00:01:39.840
The parasites that caused
the mosquito-borne disease malaria,

00:01:39.840 --> 00:01:42.360
which kills hundreds
of thousands of people a year,

00:01:42.360 --> 00:01:46.000
makes you more
attractive to, you guessed it,

00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:49.400
the mosquitoes
that transmit malaria.

00:01:49.400 --> 00:01:53.000
What better way for the parasites
to hitch from person-to-person.

00:01:53.000 --> 00:01:54.720
Instead of leaving
it up to chance,

00:01:54.720 --> 00:01:58.600
some parasites manipulate
their hosts in elaborate ways.

00:01:58.600 --> 00:02:02.520
I’ve talked about how the toxoplasma
brain parasite draws mice

00:02:02.520 --> 00:02:06.520
to the smell of cat urine
to get into cats’ brains,

00:02:06.520 --> 00:02:10.000
or how about the rabies virus
concentrating in the saliva

00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:14.240
while tapping into the Cujo
rage circuit in the brain.

00:02:14.240 --> 00:02:18.240
There’s even a parasite that needs
to get from an ant to a bird;

00:02:18.240 --> 00:02:23.160
so, it turns the ant’s belly bright
red to look like a ripe berry

00:02:23.160 --> 00:02:24.920
and makes the ant
stick it up into

00:02:24.920 --> 00:02:28.196
the air to confuse
fruit-eating bird.

00:02:28.240 --> 00:02:30.840
Just like malaria
parasites making us

00:02:30.840 --> 00:02:34.120
particularly tasty
to mosquitos.

00:02:34.120 --> 00:02:37.120
Anything we can do to make
ourselves less tasty?

00:02:37.120 --> 00:02:39.360
I’ve talked about the various
mosquito repellents

00:02:39.360 --> 00:02:40.880
you could spray on your skin,

00:02:40.880 --> 00:02:44.400
both synthetic and natural
mosquito repellents,

00:02:44.400 --> 00:02:45.560
but is there
anything you can eat

00:02:45.560 --> 00:02:48.680
or drink to make you
less of a target?

00:02:48.680 --> 00:02:52.200
When you search the scientific
literature for diet and mosquitoes,

00:02:52.200 --> 00:02:56.320
a lot of articles like this
pop up, on diets for mosquitoes,

00:02:56.320 --> 00:03:01.800
like SkitoSnack for that artificial
blood meal replacement.

00:03:01.800 --> 00:03:05.760
Feeding mice different
diets makes a difference,

00:03:05.760 --> 00:03:08.000
but what about people?

00:03:08.000 --> 00:03:09.400
One of the most
common anecdotes

00:03:09.400 --> 00:03:11.760
is that vitamin B
complex supplements

00:03:11.760 --> 00:03:13.720
protect against biting insects.

00:03:13.720 --> 00:03:17.760
Other anecdotal remedies include
the taking of garlic, marmite,

00:03:17.760 --> 00:03:21.200
vegemite, brewer’s yeast
tablets, and alcohol,

00:03:21.200 --> 00:03:26.400
but you don’t know...
until you put it to the test.

00:03:26.400 --> 00:03:28.960
How about a randomized, double-blind,
placebo-controlled trial

00:03:28.960 --> 00:03:31.160
of garlic as a mosquito repellant?

00:03:31.160 --> 00:03:32.680
A belief in the ability of garlic

00:03:32.680 --> 00:03:35.000
to repel insects seems
to be widespread;

00:03:35.000 --> 00:03:39.320
so, researchers in Connecticut
decided to see if it were true.

00:03:39.320 --> 00:03:40.920
They looked at the numbers
of mosquitoes

00:03:40.920 --> 00:03:42.760
that did not feed
on the subjects,

00:03:42.760 --> 00:03:43.920
the number of mosquito bites,

00:03:43.920 --> 00:03:45.920
the weights of the mosquitoes
after feeding,

00:03:45.920 --> 00:03:48.480
and the amount of blood
ingested were all determined

00:03:48.480 --> 00:03:50.840
on people on and off garlic,

00:03:50.840 --> 00:03:54.120
and the data did not
provide evidence

00:03:54.120 --> 00:03:57.200
of significant
mosquito repellence.

00:03:57.200 --> 00:03:59.720
No surprise given
that even if you slather

00:03:59.720 --> 00:04:01.360
garlic oil on your skin,

00:04:01.360 --> 00:04:04.920
within 30 minutes mosquitoes
don’t seem to care.

00:04:04.920 --> 00:04:09.440
Eating garlic may,
however, help against ticks.

00:04:09.440 --> 00:04:12.520
Because military personnel can
sometimes be at particularly high risk

00:04:12.520 --> 00:04:15.000
for tick bites
and tick-borne diseases,

00:04:15.000 --> 00:04:17.880
the Swedish military
conducted randomized

00:04:17.880 --> 00:04:19.520
controlled double-blind trials

00:04:19.520 --> 00:04:24.120
of garlic to prevent
tick bites among marines.

00:04:24.120 --> 00:04:27.120
Fifty swallowed the equivalent
of about a clove a day of garlic,

00:04:27.120 --> 00:04:30.360
and fifty took placebo pills;
then, they all switched.

00:04:30.360 --> 00:04:34.360
And, there was a significant
reduction in tick bites

00:04:34.360 --> 00:04:37.040
when consuming garlic
compared with placebo,

00:04:37.040 --> 00:04:41.225
cutting the risk of tick bites
by about 20 percent.

00:04:41.225 --> 00:04:43.520
Twenty percent is better than nothing,
but treating your clothing

00:04:43.520 --> 00:04:45.800
with something like
permethrin has been shown

00:04:45.800 --> 00:04:48.280
to be 100 percent effective
against deer ticks,

00:04:48.280 --> 00:04:50.400
the vector of Lyme disease, and so,

00:04:50.400 --> 00:04:55.720
that may be better than counting
on garlic bread to save you.

00:04:55.720 --> 00:04:57.080
In our next story,

00:04:57.080 --> 00:05:02.520
what happens when mosquitos
put on beer goggles?

00:05:02.520 --> 00:05:06.480
An online survey of personal
mosquito-repellent strategies

00:05:06.480 --> 00:05:09.120
unearthed all sorts
of strange stratagems

00:05:09.120 --> 00:05:13.040
from cutting a tomato in half
and leaving it next to the bed,

00:05:13.040 --> 00:05:17.240
to rubbing yourself with cigarette
butts soaked in alcohol.

00:05:17.240 --> 00:05:20.560
You could also soak yourself
in alcohol with a gin and tonic,

00:05:20.560 --> 00:05:24.840
cut down on sugar,
cut out meat, or bananas.

00:05:24.840 --> 00:05:27.360
But what’s funny
is some say avoid bananas,

00:05:27.360 --> 00:05:29.880
some say eat bananas
to stave off mosquitos,

00:05:29.880 --> 00:05:33.640
and others say topically
rub them on your skin.

00:05:33.640 --> 00:05:37.960
(I don’t even want to know about
what else you might do with them).

00:05:37.960 --> 00:05:39.880
Eat bananas? Avoid bananas?

00:05:39.880 --> 00:05:44.960
You don’t know...until
you put it to the test.

00:05:44.960 --> 00:05:47.960
The impact of the consumption
of bananas

00:05:47.960 --> 00:05:51.440
on attraction of a malaria
mosquito to humans.

00:05:51.440 --> 00:05:54.560
Researchers in Wisconsin
randomized subjects to eat grapes

00:05:54.560 --> 00:05:59.680
or bananas before testing what they
then tasted like to mosquitoes and...

00:05:59.680 --> 00:06:03.760
the ingestion of bananas was strongly
associated with an increase

00:06:03.760 --> 00:06:07.440
in the number of mosquito contacts
for hours after eating a banana,

00:06:07.440 --> 00:06:09.520
translating to about
11 extra contacts

00:06:09.520 --> 00:06:13.120
after 1 hour and 7 contacts
after 2 hours.

00:06:13.120 --> 00:06:16.520
Meanwhile, the ingestion
of grapes had no effect.

00:06:16.520 --> 00:06:18.160
Interestingly, it didn’t
seem to matter

00:06:18.160 --> 00:06:20.160
how many bananas
you eat at once,

00:06:20.160 --> 00:06:21.880
as eating three bananas
didn’t appear

00:06:21.880 --> 00:06:25.000
to make people any tastier
than eating one.

00:06:25.000 --> 00:06:27.760
Bottomline, after years
of repeat experiments,

00:06:27.760 --> 00:06:31.440
they concluded that ingestion
of bananas, but not grapes,

00:06:31.440 --> 00:06:34.440
resulted in a significantly higher
attraction of mosquitoes

00:06:34.440 --> 00:06:36.760
for hours after
ingestion on average,

00:06:36.760 --> 00:06:41.120
though some people did appear
to be immune to the banana effect.

00:06:41.120 --> 00:06:42.920
What about that gin and tonic?

00:06:42.920 --> 00:06:46.000
Some have suggested alcohol
will keep the bugs away;

00:06:46.000 --> 00:06:48.520
others suggest we might
suffer more mosquito bites

00:06:48.520 --> 00:06:50.440
after ingesting liquor.

00:06:50.440 --> 00:06:53.680
Well, there’s only
one way to find out.

00:06:53.680 --> 00:06:58.640
Drink some beer and put your arm
in a box with some mosquitoes.

00:06:58.640 --> 00:07:01.400
The title of the study
gives it away.

00:07:01.400 --> 00:07:05.080
Alcohol ingestion stimulates
mosquito attraction.

00:07:05.080 --> 00:07:07.480
About 40 percent of the mosquitoes
landed on their arms

00:07:07.480 --> 00:07:09.200
before drinking
a bottle of beer

00:07:09.200 --> 00:07:11.760
compared to about
50 percent afterwards.

00:07:11.760 --> 00:07:14.200
And it didn’t appear to have
anything to do with changes

00:07:14.200 --> 00:07:17.480
in sweat production or skin
temperature after the booze.

00:07:17.480 --> 00:07:21.000
It might just be something you
start exuding after you drink.

00:07:21.000 --> 00:07:24.320
And so, it’s also not just because
you got bit a bunch of times

00:07:24.320 --> 00:07:27.120
because you like blacked out
in an alley or something.

00:07:27.120 --> 00:07:30.000
The researchers concluded that
since the percent of mosquitos

00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:33.640
landing on volunteers significantly
increased after beer ingestion,

00:07:33.640 --> 00:07:37.240
drinking alcohol stimulates
mosquito attraction.

00:07:37.240 --> 00:07:41.240
But it could just be drinking beer,
not necessarily all alcohol.

00:07:41.240 --> 00:07:43.120
And they only tested
one species of mosquito,

00:07:43.120 --> 00:07:47.960
the one that transmits diseases like
dengue, zika, and yellow fever.

00:07:47.960 --> 00:07:51.880
What about gauging human attractiveness
to malaria mosquitoes,

00:07:51.880 --> 00:07:54.640
before and after volunteers
consumed either beer

00:07:54.640 --> 00:07:58.320
(using 25 volunteers
and a total of 2500 mosquitoes)

00:07:58.320 --> 00:08:00.640
or water as a control,

00:08:00.640 --> 00:08:05.160
with 18 volunteers and only
about 1800 mosquitoes. And..?

00:08:05.160 --> 00:08:07.080
Water consumption had no effect,

00:08:07.080 --> 00:08:11.240
but beer consumption increased
the attractiveness of the volunteers.

00:08:11.240 --> 00:08:13.920
It’s like the mosquitos
put on beer goggles.

00:08:13.920 --> 00:08:17.760
Beer consumption increases
human attractiveness.

00:08:17.760 --> 00:08:21.440
To date, bananas and beer
are the only dietary components

00:08:21.440 --> 00:08:24.800
that have been shown
to increase mosquito attraction.

00:08:24.800 --> 00:08:28.080
OK, but we want to repel
mosquitos, not attract them.

00:08:28.080 --> 00:08:29.680
What about testing
B vitamins

00:08:29.680 --> 00:08:31.920
as a home remedy
against mosquitoes?

00:08:31.920 --> 00:08:35.160
B vitamins are often
recommended in the popular media

00:08:35.160 --> 00:08:39.680
as a systemic repellent against
mosquitoes, especially on the web.

00:08:39.680 --> 00:08:42.760
The first studies date
back over a half century.

00:08:42.760 --> 00:08:46.000
They gave people doses
of vitamins B1 and B6,

00:08:46.000 --> 00:08:48.280
yet in a series of subsequent
tests the mosquitoes

00:08:48.280 --> 00:08:51.840
probed avidly
and bit promptly.

00:08:51.840 --> 00:08:53.720
They only tested
the vitamins on four people,

00:08:53.720 --> 00:08:55.600
but the vitamins
appeared so useless,

00:08:55.600 --> 00:08:57.000
they didn’t think
it worth repeating

00:08:57.000 --> 00:08:59.040
the experiments in view
of the obvious lack

00:08:59.040 --> 00:09:02.480
of repellency
of these vitamins.

00:09:02.480 --> 00:09:06.120
We believe, the researchers
wrote, that we have disproved

00:09:06.120 --> 00:09:10.040
the notions that vitamins taken
orally act as mosquito repellents.

00:09:10.040 --> 00:09:13.200
But they only tested
vitamins B1 and B6.

00:09:13.200 --> 00:09:16.400
What about B-2, B-3,
B-5, B-9, B12?

00:09:16.400 --> 00:09:20.580
You don’t know...until
you put it to the test.

00:09:20.639 --> 00:09:22.200
Vitamin B complex supplements

00:09:22.200 --> 00:09:25.560
are not effective as repellents,
but these studies were limited

00:09:25.560 --> 00:09:27.760
by the use of very
few human subjects,

00:09:27.760 --> 00:09:31.680
only 1 species of mosquito,
and a limited number of B vitamins.

00:09:31.680 --> 00:09:35.160
So, researchers decided to put
it to rest once and for all.

00:09:35.160 --> 00:09:40.680
B-1, B-2, B-3, B-5, B-6, B-7,
also known as biotin, B-9, B12.

00:09:40.680 --> 00:09:44.280
They also just tried
a mega-dose of thiamine, B1,

00:09:44.280 --> 00:09:49.080
which is rumored to be the most
effective B and...nothing.

00:09:49.080 --> 00:09:51.480
No effect of vitamin B
supplementation.

00:09:51.480 --> 00:09:53.560
Any of them.
I mean it would be nice

00:09:53.560 --> 00:09:56.200
to have an effective
oral insect repellent.

00:09:56.200 --> 00:10:00.960
Unfortunately, vitamin B1
has been proved to be ineffective.

00:10:00.960 --> 00:10:03.480
And this includes so-called
mosquito repellent patches,

00:10:03.480 --> 00:10:06.000
that supposedly deliver
B1 through the skin.

00:10:06.000 --> 00:10:08.600
No protection
provided whatsoever.

00:10:08.600 --> 00:10:11.800
Bottomline: Vitamin B1,
also known as thiamine,

00:10:11.800 --> 00:10:15.440
is not a systemic
mosquito repellent in men.

00:10:15.440 --> 00:10:18.480
They also tried smearing
it on people’s skin.

00:10:18.480 --> 00:10:20.400
With failure after failure,

00:10:20.400 --> 00:10:22.760
you start feeling bad
for the volunteers,

00:10:22.760 --> 00:10:25.320
seated in a room
with their shirts off.

00:10:25.320 --> 00:10:27.980
Then, they just release
100 suckers into the room.

00:10:28.013 --> 00:10:30.880
Up to 96 bites per minute.

00:10:30.880 --> 00:10:32.840
Just think how bad
it would have been

00:10:32.840 --> 00:10:37.600
if they had had some
bananas and beer.

00:10:37.600 --> 00:10:39.880
